' F11 -- LLM provider failover chain and its correlated-failure flaw.
' Chapter 4. UML activity diagram.
' Claim supported: the chain presents nine providers but contains roughly five
' independent failure domains; failure classification is three-way and omits
' the authentication and payment classes entirely.
@startuml f11-provider-chain
!include _style.iuml

title LLM provider failover -- nine entries, ~five failure domains

start
:call site\n(BULK or QUALITY chain);

if (per-user monthly budget OK?) then (no)
  #DCDCDC:LLMBudgetExceededError;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:refresh fleet-wide counters from Redis;
:move user-preferred provider to head of chain;

partition "Availability filter (in order)" {
  :skip if not in registry;
  :skip if permanently disabled;
  :skip if no API key configured;
  :skip if fleet daily cost ceiling hit (OpenAI);
  :skip if daily request limit reached;
  :skip if inside backoff window;
}

while (providers remaining?) is (yes)
  :call provider;
  if (outcome?) then (success)
    :record success, flush counter,\naccount cost;
    #BFBFBF:return response;
    stop
  elseif (429 / "rate limit" / "quota") then
    :exponential backoff\n90s x 2^n, capped 600s;
  elseif (404 model not found) then
    :**permanent** disable\n//not cleared at UTC midnight//;
  else (401 / 402 / 403 / 5xx / network)
    #DCDCDC:**no penalty recorded**;
    note right
      A revoked key or exhausted credit
      balance re-fires a doomed HTTPS
      request on every subsequent call
      for the whole process lifetime.
      There is no 402 handling anywhere
      in the codebase.
    end note
  endif
endwhile (no)

#DCDCDC:raise last exception;
stop

note right
  **Three weaknesses to discuss.**

  1. Chain depth is partly illusory.
     'gemma' is not Gemma -- its model is
     gemini-2.0-flash-lite, sharing one
     GEMINI_API_KEY with the 'gemini' entry.
     Same for groq_fast / groq. Four of nine
     entries are **not** independent failure
     domains, so their separate daily quotas
     (14 400 vs 1 500) are fiction.

  2. Classification is string-sniffing on
     str(exc).lower(), not status codes. A
     prompt containing the word "quota" can
     be misclassified as a rate limit.

  3. The retry budget is unreachable.
     stop_after_attempt(8) with
     wait_exponential(min=4, max=60) sits
     inside asyncio.wait_for(timeout=25s).
     4+8+16s already exceeds 25s, capping
     real attempts near three. The docstring
     says "3x"; the code says 8.
end note

legend bottom
  BULK:    cerebras > groq_fast > cloudflare > gemma > mistral > openrouter > gemini > groq > openai
  QUALITY: cerebras > groq > openrouter > cloudflare > gemini > mistral > groq_fast > gemma > openai
  Vision uses a separate three-provider chain that does not classify 404 at all.
endlegend

@enduml
